# Stage 6A.90. Before this, line endings and BOMs were inconsistent across the
# repository - MainWindow.xaml was CRLF, MainWindow.xaml.cs was LF, MainViewModel.cs
# was CRLF with a BOM - with no rule saying which was correct. Nothing was broken by
# it, but a patch written against the wrong convention does not error, it silently
# matches nothing, which cost two build cycles. One convention now, enforced by git.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shell scripts must keep CRLF or they will not run.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Binary.
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary

# Evidence, not source. These are genuine Ctrl+S browser saves and the parser
# records that a real save begins with the browser's "saved from url" comment and
# nothing else, and two files in that folder were once reconstructions passed off as
# real saves. Marked -text so git never rewrites a byte of them in either direction.
tests/CardFactory.ProfitLoss.ReportParsing.Tests/Fixtures/** -text
